\chapter{Future work}

The potential of latent disentanglement in computational photography lies in problems where the values of the salient factors are unavailable, or difficult to express explicitly. The prototypical image synthesis problem requiring disentangled representations is the general ``fusion'' task, which involves generating a new image by combining some of the factors extracted from one image with the remaining factors extracted from another image. Two high-level image editing problems interest me in particular: changing the ``style'' of an image while preserving a coherent structure, and inserting/removing/modifying objects in a scene.

